NativeXRenderer: make the swap chain on the game's window work outside Windows.

device.cpp's non-Windows path passes an empty NativeWindow to
CreateSwapChainVk, so the swap chain (and with it the renderer) can never
start on Android - NativeXRenderer is Windows-first. On Android NativeWindow
is AndroidNativeWindow, whose one field is the ANativeWindow that
WindowSDL::GetNativeWindowHandle() returns (the SDK's window_sdl.cpp).

The submodule stays pristine: this patch is applied to its working tree at
build time (android/build.sh, ios/build.sh), the way NativeXRenderer applies
its own diligent_patches at configure time and the original project applies
android/patches/rexglue-sdk-v0.10.0-*.patch.
diff --git a/src/device.cpp b/src/device.cpp
index a0406c9..f2aeb1a 100644
--- a/src/device.cpp
+++ b/src/device.cpp
@@ -104,6 +104,11 @@ bool Device::Create(void* native_window) {
   swap_chain_desc.BufferCount = 3;
 #ifdef _WIN32
   Win32NativeWindow window{static_cast<HWND>(native_window)};
+#elif defined(__ANDROID__)
+  // The game's window: the SDL window's ANativeWindow, which
+  // WindowSDL::GetNativeWindowHandle() returns. The empty default below
+  // cannot make a VkSurface.
+  NativeWindow window{native_window};
 #else
   NativeWindow window{};
 #endif
